Task 23 — Dockerized Application & Dual Local Development Workflow

Goal

Add Docker support so Snapland GIS supports two simple startup modes from the SAME docker-compose.yml:

1. Complete application — default/reproducible mode

       docker compose up --build

   Starts:

       PostgreSQL/PostGIS
       Redis
       Spring Boot backend
       Angular frontend

2. Infrastructure-only — normal active development

       docker compose up -d postgres redis

   Starts only:

       PostgreSQL/PostGIS
       Redis

   The developer then runs backend/frontend directly on the host using IntelliJ/Maven and npm.

Do NOT use Docker Compose profiles.

Do NOT create duplicate Compose files merely to support these two modes.

The existing fast local development workflow must remain fully supported.

Before making changes, inspect the actual current:

- docker-compose.yml
- backend configuration
- frontend configuration
- Angular build configuration/output
- Spring profiles
- ports
- environment variables
- REST URLs
- CORS configuration
- WebSocket/STOMP configuration
- Swagger configuration from Task 22

Do not guess paths, ports, property names, Angular dist locations, or WebSocket endpoints.

