## 1. Required startup modes

### Complete application

The primary reproducible/demo startup command must be:

    docker compose up --build

It must start:

    postgres
    redis
    backend
    frontend

After startup, the user should be able to open:

    http://localhost:4201

and use the application.

This is the expected workflow for:

- first-time project startup
- reviewer/demo usage
- clean-start verification
- machines with Docker but without locally installed Java/Node/PostgreSQL

### Infrastructure-only development

The recommended active-development command must be:

    docker compose up -d postgres redis

This must start only:

    postgres
    redis

Backend is then run directly:

    cd backend
    ./mvnw spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev

Frontend is then run directly:

    cd frontend
    npm start

This workflow must preserve:

- IntelliJ debugging
- Java breakpoints
- fast backend restart
- Angular hot reload
- normal frontend development tooling

Docker must NOT become mandatory for running backend/frontend during active development.

