Docker Compose Service Structure

postgres   — postgis/postgis:16-3.4 (amd64, emulated on Apple Silicon)
redis      — redis:7-alpine (multi-arch)
backend    — eclipse-temurin:21-jre (multi-arch), port 8081
frontend   — nginx:alpine (multi-arch), port 4201

REST Proxy Strategy

nginx receives all browser traffic on port 4201. Requests to /api/* are forwarded to http://backend:8081/ with the /api/ prefix stripped (matching what the Angular dev proxy does in development). The Angular production build uses apiUrl: '/api' which is identical to the development environment — no code path differs between the two modes.

WebSocket Proxy Strategy

nginx proxies /ws to http://backend:8081/ws with proxy_http_version 1.1, Upgrade, and Connection: upgrade headers. In the production build, wsUrl is empty and realtime.service.ts derives the URL from window.location.host, producing ws://localhost:4201/ws when served by nginx and ws://localhost:8081/ws when served by the Angular dev server (override via environment.ts).

